       "content": "# Game Engines for Web-Based Games\n\n## \ud83c\udfc6 Top Tier (Most Recommended)\n\n### 1. **Godot**\n- **Type:** Full game engine (2D & 3D)\n- **Export:** WebAssembly (WASM)\n- **License:** MIT (fully open source)\n\n**Pros:**\n- Completely free, no royalties, no corporate ownership\n- Lightweight exports (smaller than Unity's WebGL builds)\n- Excellent 2D support (one of the best)\n- Growing community and documentation\n- GDScript is easy to learn; also supports C#\n- Actively developed by a community, not a corporation\n\n**Cons:**\n- 3D is good but not on par with Unity/Unreal\n- WASM exports can be slower than native JS frameworks\n- Smaller asset store compared to Unity\n- Some plugins/tools are still maturing\n\n**Longevity Outlook:** \u2b50\u2b50\u2b50\u2b50\u2b50 \u2014 Open source, community-driven, no corporate risk\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Phaser**\n- **Type:** 2D JavaScript game framework\n- **Export:** Native web (runs",
